  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 158 AM MDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nHigh pressure is building in over parts of the West today and will \nmove directly over our area on Friday. This means we can expect dry \nconditions for the next several days and a warming trend is \nunderway. While temperatures will start in the low to mid 30s for \nmost this morning, we warm into the upper 50s and low 60s this \nafternoon. Highs warm a few more degrees for Friday and Saturday \nafternoons and Saturday looks the be the warmest day for most with \nhighs in the low to mid 60s. This warm up has backed off a little \nbit from what it looked like the last few days where now, there's \nonly about a 25 percent chance that areas around Burley reach 70 \ndegrees for the high on Saturday. \n\nDuring the first half of next week, an upper level low drops \nsouthward along the West Coast. Now, the ECMWF and GFS have very \ndifferent solutions on where exactly this low will track and how \nquickly it will move. However, it does seem like we will see \nincreasing precipitation chances in the second half of next week \nthanks to this system along with some cooler temperatures meaning \nhighs back in the 50s.",
